// workspace_topology.proto — WHERE A NEW WORKSPACE'S WORK COMES FROM AND
// GOES: the branch it is cut from, the branch it lands in, and the
// conversation it starts with. Shared by every rpc that makes a workspace
// (CreateWorkspace, in each of its forms).
//
// THREE CHOICES, EACH ALWAYS MADE. A create names its branch source and merge
// target (one topology arm names both) and its context origin; none of them has
// a default, so every create is a specific, intentional one.
//
// THE OWNERSHIP RULE, which the topology arms make structural: a branch cut
// from the primary branch lands only on the primary branch, and a branch a
// workspace owns lands only into that workspace. A workspace is therefore never
// cut from one owner's branch and landed in another's; no arm can express it.
// The one way work on a branch no workspace owns reaches anything is the async
// merge (CreateWorkspaceAsyncMerge), whose source and target are its own.

